The current selection criterion minimizes the *current* GPU KVPR before placing a model, rather than the KVPR that results *after* the placement. This can send a large/high-pressure model to a GPU that becomes highly congested immediately afterward.

The replacement below:
- evaluates the resulting KVPR for every candidate GPU;
- tries both KV-weight-first and memory-size-first orderings;
- retains the better feasible greedy placement;
- performs inexpensive improving single-model moves from the most congested GPU.

